35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The tin holds 2,300 yen monthly, mostly duplicates. The office rates cleaners at 4,200 yen per hour, billed to one tenant.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The timing shows one hundred and two minutes total. The firm requires someone present to tidy beforehand. Outsourcing doesn’t remove the hours; it just shifts them to supervision.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The data is damning. Two or three people create the mess, yet the calendar shows two are gone for weeks. The labor doesn't match the usage.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"So the grout fails in eleven days, and ""done"" means whatever the last person decided. That explains the chaos.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, the previous tenants’ note confirms permanent splits breed silence. The chat shows reminders spark our rows. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, your timing confirms the cost. At 4,200 yen an hour, a full pass costs over 70,000 yen. That is unsustainable for us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the math is wrong. One hundred and two minutes is under two hours. The real cost is the two-hour window and the prep work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, the math is irrelevant if the labor is misallocated. The heavy users are rarely here, yet the absent ones count equally. That is the core failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the grout data proves the room is a trap. No matter who cleans, it fails in eleven days. We need a standard that accounts for that reality.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, the previous tenants’ silence proves permanent splits fail. We need a system that prevents reminders from becoming rows, keeping us on speaking terms.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the 4,200 yen rate is the floor. Add the 2,300 yen supplies and the one-tenant billing risk, and the monthly out-of-pocket is significant.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the cost is secondary. The firm’s terms mean I must still be present to tidy. I am not outsourcing my time; I am adding a management layer to it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, you’re right about the prep. But my data shows the mess is concentrated. If we fix the allocation, the hours drop. I need to see the usage pattern.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, fixing allocation doesn't fix the grout. It fails in eleven days regardless of who scrubs. I need a standard that accepts that reality.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. The previous tenants’ silence shows permanent splits fail. We need a system that prevents reminders from becoming rows, keeping us on speaking terms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
